SUMMARY:'Quin Chat\; Behind the Curtain - To Kill a Mockingbird
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 11 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/203290\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nExperience a behind-th
 e-curtain look as The Huntington Theatre Company prepares to present the 
 first regional production of Aaron Sorkin’s acclaimed adaptation of To 
 Kill a Mockingbird. Artistic Director and Director of the production\, Lor
 etta Greco joins fellow members of the production to explore the art and c
 omplexity of bringing Harper Lee’s enduring classic to the stage\, reve
 aling what audiences rarely see: the journey from script to stage\, the ar
 tistic decisions made along the way\, and the collaboration required to br
 ing a production of this scale to life. Together\, they will consider the
  delicate balance between honoring a story that has resonated for generati
 ons and embracing the creative freedom and fresh perspective that come wit
 h a new interpretation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for m
 embers only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We
  kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the 
 start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203290
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
